WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.209
It looks like Chris Pratt just posted a major
spoiler for Avengers 4 online.

00:00:05.209 --> 00:00:06.680
"Oh I'm sorry.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.460
I didn't know how this machine worked."

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.950
We're jumping into the spoilers for Avengers:
Infinity War right away, so now's your last

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.120
chance to bail.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:15.840
Still here?

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:16.980
"Let's go."

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:21.820
Stephen McFeely and Christopher Markus, the
screenwriters of Avengers: Infinity War and

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:26.440
Avengers 4: Even More Infinity War Than Before,
have stuck to their guns in saying that the

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:30.820
heart-squeezing deaths you saw in the theater
are real, saying: "the sooner you accept that,

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.850
the sooner you will be able to move on to
the next stage of grief."

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:37.550
But in all honesty, fans know better than
to listen to that crappy advice.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:42.440
And thanks to an accidental slip from Star-Lord
actor Chris Pratt, their optimistic judgement

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.800
has seemingly been proven right.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.490
In a recent Instagram post, it appears Pratt
spoiled a part of Avengers 4 by confirming

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:55.000
the fates of Star-Lord and Pom Klementieff's
Mantis, both of whom disintegrated into space

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.920
ash after Thanos snapped his Infinity Gauntlet-wearing
hand and got rid of half of the universe's

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.100
inhabitants.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.850
Many believed that most of the deaths in Infinity
War would be reversed in Avengers 4, and Pratt

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.110
has essentially confirmed that hunch.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:11.870
So how exactly did Pratt potentially spoil
the events of Avengers 4?

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:17.280
In the most wholesome way imaginable: by wishing
Klementieff a happy birthday on Instagram,

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.320
mentioning that he's eager for the two of
them to join forces again for the third Guardians

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.659
movie in 2019.

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:23.659
He wrote:

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:27.700
"Happy birthday, Pom Klementieff, whom many
of you know as Mantis!

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.990
She's such a unique, talented, and driven
artist.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.340
Can't wait to start shooting Guardians Vol.
3 with her next year!

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:35.960
Hope you're having a good day, Pom!"

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.140
Of course, let's be real here: it was pretty
much a given that Star-Lord and Mantis would

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.630
return from the grave, since Guardians film
franchise director James Gunn has been candid

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:48.380
about the fact that Guardians of the Galaxy
Vol. 3 is a done deal.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:52.590
Tom Holland's Spider-Man, who disintegrated
in Iron Man's arms at the end of Infinity

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:56.900
War, is basically guaranteed to come back
to life as well, since he has an untitled

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:00.020
Spider-Man: Homecoming sequel in the works.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:05.899
Both Guardians Vol. 3 and the Homecoming follow-up
will launch after Avengers 4, so Star-Lord,

00:02:05.899 --> 00:02:10.319
Mantis, and Spidey, plus a few other fallen
favorites, will likely be resurrected in the

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:13.459
film before jumping back into their individual
film series.

00:02:13.459 --> 00:02:17.720
At least there's a bright side to Pratt's
accidental plot detail reveal: Tom Holland

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.730
isn't alone in spoiling Marvel movies any
longer.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:24.189
"I have been asking for weeks and weeks if
I can read the script, and every time they're

00:02:24.189 --> 00:02:25.189
like 'Nope, because you can't keep a secret.'"

00:02:25.189 --> 00:02:27.529
"They just know he's gonna talk about it."

00:02:27.529 --> 00:02:28.529
Thanks for watching!

00:02:28.529 --> 00:02:30.829
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:02:30.829 --> 00:02:33.489
Plus, check out this other cool stuff we know
you'll love too!

